  "text": "{\"query\":\"CC(=O)[O-].COc1cc(C=O)ccc1Cl.[NH4+]>>COc1cc(C=C(C)[N+](=O)[O-])ccc1Cl\",\"results\":[{\"reactants\":\"CC(=O)[O-].COc1ccc(C=O)cc1OCc1ccccc1.[NH4+]\",\"products\":\"COc1ccc(/C=C(\\\\C)[N+](=O)[O-])cc1OCc1ccccc1\",\"solvents\":\"CCO.CCOC(C)=O\",\"reagents\":\"CC[N+](=O)[O-]\",\"experiments_details\":\" 3-Benzyloxy-4-methoxybenzaldehyde (8.0 g, 33.05 mmol), ammonium acetate (2.55 g, 33.05 mmol) and nitroethane (120 ml) were stirred under reflux for 22 h. The reaction mixture was cooled to rt and nitroethane was removed in vacuo. The solid residue was dissolved in ethyl acetate (200 ml), washed with water (40 ml) and brine (2×40 ml), dried ( MgSO₄) and concentrated in vacuo. Recrystallisation from ethanol afforded the title compound (6.19 g, 63%) as yellow crystals. mp=102-104°C.¹H NMR (270 MHz; CDCl₃) 2.27 (3H, s, CH₃), 3.94 (3H, s, OCH₃), 5.19 (2H, s, CH₂Ph), 6.91 (1H, d, J=2.0 Hz, CH), 6.94 (1H, d, J=8.4 Hz, CH), 7.05 (1H, dd, J=8.4, 2.0 Hz, CH), 7.30-7.43 (4H, m, 4×CH), 7.97 (1H, s, CH).¹³C NMR (67.5 MHz; CDCl₃) 14.03 (CH₃), 56.15 (OCH₃), 71.25 (CH₂Ph), 111.69 (CH), 115.77 (CH), 124.93 (C), 124.94 (CH), 127.16 (CH), 128.19 (CH), 128.83 (CH), 133.84 (CH), 136.65 (C), 145.92 (C), 148.00 (C), 151.51 (C). LC/MS (APCI−) tᵣ=1.07 min, m/z 297.93 (M−H)⁻. \",\"file_name\":\"US20100222299\"},{\"reactants\":\"CCc1ccc(C=O)cc1OC\",\"products\":\"CCC(=Cc1ccc(CC)c(OC)c1)[N+](=O)[O-]\",\"solvents\":\"CCOC(C)=O\",\"reagents\":\"CC(=O)[O-].CCC[N+](=O)[O-].[NH4+]\",\"experiments_details\":\" A mixture of 4-ethyl-3-methoxy-benzaldehyde (2 g, 12.4 mmol) and ammonium acetate (950 mg, 12.4 mmol) in nitropropane (20 mL) was refluxed for 3 hours. The mixture was concentrated under reduced pressure, and the residue was dissolved in ethyl acetate (20 mL). The resultant solution was washed with water (20 mL), and then dried over anhydrous Na₂SO₄ and then concentrated. The residue was purified by column chromatography to give 1-ethyl-2-methoxy-4-[2-nitrobut-1-enyl]benzene (2.3 g). \",\"file_name\":\"US20160296515\"},{\"reactants\":\"CC(=O)[O-].O=Cc1ccc(Cl)c(OCc2ccccc2)c1.[NH4+]\",\"products\":\"O=[N+]([O-])C=Cc1ccc(Cl)c(OCc2ccccc2)c1\",\"solvents\":\"C[N+](=O)[O-]\",\"reagents\":\"CC(=O)O\",\"experiments_details\":\" A mixture of 3-benzyloxy-4-chloro-benzaldehyde compound, 2, (20 mmol), ammonium acetate (22 mL of 60 mmol in nitromethane) and 6 mL acetic acid was heated for 3 h. The reaction mixture was cooled down to rt and left overnight. A crystalline material formed, which was filtered and washed with a small amount of EtOAc and hexane to give a yellow product. The mother liquid was concentrated, dissolved in chloroform, washed with water and brine and dried. The material formed from the mother liquid was concentrated and purified by chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc:Hexane=1:3) to give more of the yellow product as a light yellow solid, 2-benzyloxy-1-chloro-4-(2-nitro-vinyl)-benzene, 3. \",\"file_name\":\"US20080287516\"}]}"
